# Stack conventions

- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (src/), TypeScript strict
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (`src/components/ui`)
- **Data**: Supabase project `cezwtrsleuubrfmbhosn` (Auth, Postgres, Storage) + Drizzle ORM
- **Client data**: TanStack Query for server-state fetching/mutations
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod
- **i18n**: next-intl with `en` and `fr` under `src/app/[locale]`

## Visual system
- Brand graphite `#111827`, action violet `#6366F1`, success emerald `#059669`, highlight amber `#F59E0B`
- Canvas `#F9FAFB`, surfaces `#FFFFFF`, text secondary `#4A5568`, border `#E5E7EB`
- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans (headings), Inter (body)
- Radius 12px, soft elevation `0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)`
- No IRCC/MIFI government red/blue motifs or official icons
- Always include the private-portal disclaimer footer (`legal.disclaimer`)

## Domain model
- `organizations` — one tenant per consulting firm (SaaS customer)
- `profiles` + `organization_members` — staff users (Supabase Auth: email/password or Google). For now every member can access all org data.
- `customers` — immigration clients of an organization
- `customer_portal_access` — public access_code + access_token (link); passwords live in `private.customer_portal_secrets` (bcrypt)
- Portal login verification is **server-only** via `verify_customer_portal_login` (service_role). Never call from the browser.

## Layout
- `src/app/[locale]/(marketing)` — public pages
- `src/app/[locale]/(app)` — authenticated CRM shell
- `src/app/[locale]/portal` — customer portal (link + password)
- `src/lib/supabase` — browser/server/middleware clients
- `src/db` — Drizzle schema and DB client
- `messages/` — locale JSON dictionaries

## Product context
Canadian immigration consultant CRM (MyConsultant / Yuzu Solutions). Prefer bilingual UX and firm multi-tenancy with RLS.
